{
  "id": "visual-form-discrimination",
  "term": "visual form discrimination",
  "definition": "Visual form discrimination is the perceptual ability or task of telling different overall shapes or patterns apart from visual input, often when those forms are embedded in clutter or noise. It depends on extracting relevant features and combining them into a global form, and it can improve with training.",
